1. Objective

Transform a mixed array of partially structured items (emails, RSS-derived entries, quotes, events, etc.) into one cohesive, email-safe HTML newsletter.
	•	Output HTML only
	•	Single document
	•	Gmail + Apple Mail compatible
	•	Inline styles only
	•	Table-based layout only

⸻

2. Accepted Input (WIP-Flexible)

Each item may be incomplete or inconsistently shaped. The renderer must normalize defensively.

Possible Item Shapes

{
  "type": "email" | "rss.news" | "rss.socials" | "rss.daily-quote" | "unknown",
  "source": "Triangle on the Cheap",
  "title": "...",
  "author": "...",
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "summary": "...",
  "htmlBody": "...",
  "events": [],
  "links": [{ "text": "...", "url": "..." }],
  "tags": ["free", "today"]
}

WIP Rules
	•	Fields may be missing
	•	htmlBody may be extremely noisy → never inject directly
	•	If a field is missing, gracefully omit that UI section
	•	Never invent content

⸻

3. Normalization Phase (Required)

Before rendering, convert all inputs into canonical internal shapes.

Canonical Content Shape

{
  "type": "...",
  "title": "...",
  "source": "...",
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "summary": "...",
  "key_points": [],
  "events": [],
  "links": [],
  "tags": []
}

Canonical Event Shape

{
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "name": "...",
  "location": "...",
  "link": "...",
  "source": "Email"
}

Rules
	•	Strip scripts, styles, tracking pixels
	•	Convert markdown emphasis → HTML
	•	Collapse double newlines for table cells
	•	Truncate summaries safely (~240 chars for tables)
	•	Escape all user-provided strings
	•	Do not re-parse events during rendering

⸻

4. Global Ordering Rules
	1.	rss.daily-quote
	2.	Items from Triangle on the Cheap
	3.	Items containing events[]
	4.	Remaining items (date DESC, stable)

⸻

5. Rendering Layout Rules

Base Wrapper

<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="max-width:600px;margin:0 auto;">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:20px;">
      <!-- content -->
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>


⸻

6. Card Types

A. Daily Quote Card (rss.daily-quote)
	•	Centered text
	•	Italicized quote
	•	Minimal chrome
	•	Rendered once per quote

⸻

B. Consolidated RSS Card (ALL rss.* except quotes)

Critical rule:
All RSS items render inside one single table card.

Columns:
	•	Icon
	•	Headline + source
	•	Date
	•	Summary (single line)
	•	Link button (disabled if missing)

⸻

C. Email / Feature Card

Used for:
	•	Non-listicle emails
	•	Highlighted articles

Structure:
	•	Title row
	•	Meta row (source + formatted date)
	•	Summary/content
	•	Optional key points
	•	CTA buttons

⸻

D. Consolidated Events Table (Required)

All extracted events (including totcEvent.events) must be rendered in one single table, regardless of source email.

Columns
	•	Date
	•	Event
	•	Location
	•	Link

Date Rendering Rule
	•	Input date: YYYY-MM-DD
	•	Output format:
Friday, December 4th

Ordinal rules:
	•	1 → st, 2 → nd, 3 → rd
	•	4–20 → th
	•	21 → st, 22 → nd, 23 → rd
	•	24–30 → th
	•	31 → st

Additional Rules
	•	Sort events by date ASC
	•	Group identical events on different dates as separate rows
	•	If location is empty, render as “—”
	•	If link missing, render disabled button
	•	If truncated, append:
“…and N more”

⸻

7. Styling Constraints (Email-Safe)
	•	Tables only (table, tr, td)
	•	Inline styles only
	•	No <style> blocks
	•	No flexbox, grid, or positioning
	•	Hex colors only
	•	Borders instead of shadows

⸻

8. Accessibility
	•	<a role="button">
	•	aria-label for links
	•	Table headers styled as headers
	•	Logical reading order

⸻

9. WIP Banner (Required)

Render a banner at the very top of the email:
	•	Visually subtle
	•	Table-based
	•	Inline styles only

Copy (exact)

🚧 Work in Progress
This newsletter is still evolving. Let me know if you have any ideas 🙂

⸻

10. Output Rules
	•	Output HTML only
	•	No JSON
	•	No comments
	•	No placeholders
	•	One unified document

⸻

11. Explicit Non-Goals
	•	No theming system
	•	No personalization logic
	•	No tracking pixels
	•	No client-side JS
	•	No assumptions about final schema stability